===Etymology===
{{inh+|en|enm|pykeaxe}}, {{m|enm|pecaxe}}, {{m|enm|pyke exe|t=pickaxe}}, an alteration (due to folk etymology association with {{m|en|pick}} and {{m|en|axe}}) of {{m+|enm|pikeyse}}, {{m|enm|pikeys}}, {{m|enm|pykois}}, from {{der|en|xno|*pikeis}}, {{der|en|fro|picois}}, {{m|fro|pecois}}, from {{der|en|la|picōsa|t=pickaxe}}, from {{m|la|picca}}, ultimately from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*pīk|t=sharp point, pike}}. {{doublet|en|pique|pike}}.

